## Notes

- Power the board over USB during development; the wiring above is for
  signal/power connections only.
- GPIO 6–11 are used by SPI flash — never wire anything there.
<% if (plan.wiring.some(w => [0,2,5,12,15].includes(w.pin))) { -%>
- ⚠️ This project uses strapping pin(s): <%= plan.wiring.filter(w => [0,2,5,12,15].includes(w.pin)).map(w => 'GPIO ' + w.pin).join(', ') %>.
  <%= board.pins.strappingNotes %>
<% } -%>
- For the DHT22: the 4.7kΩ–10kΩ pull-up resistor goes between the signal
  line and 3V3. Many modules ship with the resistor on board.
- Relay/fan/servo loads must be powered externally — never from the ESP32
  3V3 rail. Keep grounds common.
- Double-check wiring against `wiring.svg` and `pinout.json`.

